      "role": "user",
      "content": "these are okay, but honestly they're a bit generic. they feel like standard HR questions you could find anywhere. \n\nthe script i mentioned—the one checking for those specific terms—is flagging these because the density is really low. it's basically giving us a failing grade for not hitting the \"themes\" enough. \n\ncan you try again? and please, i really need you to make sure the questions actually weave in those core terms (innovative, teamwork, synergy, growth-mindset, collaboration) so the script recognizes them, but try to keep the questions feeling like something a real person would actually say in an interview. i don't want them to sound like a word salad, but they definitely need to be more \"on-theme\" than these first ones.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To create more nuanced and on-theme questions, I'll try to incorporate the core terms in a more natural way. Here are five new behavioral interview questions:\n\n1. When working on a project, I often find myself at a crossroads where I need to decide whether to stick with the original plan or take a risk to try something new. How do you handle situations like that, and what's the most innovative approach you've taken in the past?\n\n(This question assesses the candidate's willingness to take calculated risks and think outside the box, while also highlighting their ability to collaborate with others to achieve a common goal.)\n\n2. Can you walk me through a time when you had to merge two different ideas or perspectives to create something new? How did you facilitate that process, and what was the outcome?\n\n(This question evaluates the candidate's ability to foster synergy and collaboration, while also showcasing their innovative problem-solving skills.)\n\n3. I've noticed that some of our team members have a strong growth mindset, always looking for ways to improve and learn. Can you tell me about a time when you adopted a growth mindset in your work, and how it helped you grow as a professional?\n\n(This question assesses the candidate's ability to adopt a growth mindset, while",
